   "id": "gate-charge-test",
   "title": "Gate charge test circuit",
   "page": 6,
   "description": "Used for Qg, Qgs and Qgd. A gate current pulse Ig charges the gate of the device under test while its gate voltage is recorded against delivered charge. Drain current flows from the Vds supply through a second N-channel MOSFET stacked above the DUT; that transistor's gate is set by a potentiometer across its own floating DC source, which is referred to the node between the two transistors, with a capacitor across the source and another from the wiper to that node. In the resulting VGS-versus-charge trace, rising to 10 V, Qgs is the charge up to the flat plateau, Qgd the charge across the plateau, and Qg the whole charge to the end voltage. The table's charge rows use VGS = 10 V, VDS = 30 V, ID = 17 A.",
