   "description": "Used for the avalanche ratings. The DUT drain is fed through the inductor L from a node that a switch connects to the Vdd supply; a diode runs from ground to that node, and a second diode sits across the switch. The DUT gate is pulsed through Rg. While the gate is high, drain current ramps up through L; when the gate falls, the inductor drives the drain into avalanche, Vds stands at BVDSS and the current decays from IAR to zero. A current sensor in the drain lead reads Id. The energy taken in avalanche is EAR = ½ L IAR². The table rates IAS = 17 A and EAS = 43 mJ at L = 0.3 mH.",
