 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Technology and uses",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "A 60 V N-channel power MOSFET built on AOS's AlphaSGT trench power process, with low on-resistance, low gate charge and an ESD-protected gate. Named uses are high-efficiency power supplies and synchronous rectification on a converter's secondary side."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Gate drive",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Threshold is 1.4 to 2.4 V (1.8 V typical) at 250 µA. On-resistance is specified at two drive levels: 9.5 mΩ max at 10 V and 17 A, 13.3 mΩ max at 4.5 V and 15 A. Total gate charge to 10 V is 14.5 nC typical, 25 nC max; to 4.5 V it is 7 nC typical, 13 nC max. Internal gate resistance is 0.6 to 2.0 Ω. The gate holds ±20 V and carries HBM Class 2 ESD protection, with ±10 µA max leakage at ±20 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Temperature",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "On-resistance climbs with junction temperature: at 10 V and 17 A it is 7.7 mΩ typical (9.5 mΩ max) at 25 °C and 12.5 mΩ typical (15.5 mΩ max) at 125 °C; Figure 4 reaches about 1.8 times the 25 °C figure at 150 °C. Below a crossing near 3.1 V gate drive the 125 °C transfer curve carries more current than the 25 °C one; above the crossing the order reverses."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Current and power limits",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The 28 A continuous rating at TC = 25 °C, and the 28 A body-diode rating, are set by the package. With the case at 100 °C the limit is 25 A and 11 W. Referred to ambient the limits are IDSM 17 A and PDSM 5.0 W at TA = 25 °C, 13.5 A and 3.2 W at 70 °C; PDSM rests on the t ≤ 10 s junction-to-ambient resistance on a 1 in² FR-4 board. Figures 12 and 13 derate power linearly to zero at 150 °C case and hold current at 28 A up to about 85 °C case."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Avalanche and voltage spikes",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Each unit is avalanche tested. Single-pulse ratings are 17 A and 43 mJ at 0.3 mH, limited by a 150 °C junction. Drain-source spikes up to 72 V lasting 10 µs are allowed at 5 % duty or less, with the junction kept to 125 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Pulsed operation",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "The 80 A pulsed rating is single-pulse, limited by a 150 °C junction. Figures 9 to 11 give safe operating area, single-pulse power and transient impedance referred to the case with the device on a large heatsink; Figures 14 and 15 give single-pulse power and transient impedance referred to ambient on the 1 in² FR-4 board. The safe-operating-area curves hold for gate drive of 4.5 V or more."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Body diode",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The source-drain diode drops 0.72 V typical, 1 V max, at 1 A. Recovery from 17 A at 500 A/µs takes 19 ns and 65 nC typical."
  }
 ]
